<section class="section" id="convenings"><div class="wrap">
<div class="section-head"><div><h2>Convenings</h2><p>Conferences, summits and working sessions the Foundation has hosted or co-hosted since 2019, from Detroit to Kyiv. Planning something for the community? <a href="https://forms.gle/YtQABdjoGtovPrHo6">Tell us</a>.</p></div></div>
<p class="year">2025</p><ul class="list"><li><a href="/events/2025-ukraine/">The Future of Digital Democracy: Learning with Ukraine</a><span class="desc">A global conversation on democratic resilience and frontline innovation in decentralised governance.</span><span class="meta">Online</span></li><li><a href="/events/2025-maine/">Foundations for the Digital Commons</a><span class="desc">Two days with leaders, builders, lawyers and technologists on tech, policy and digital infrastructure for the common good.</span><span class="meta">Maine</span></li><li><a href="/events/2025-berlin/">New Solidarity for an AI-Disrupted Economy</a><span class="desc">With the Global Solutions Initiative and Sciences Po, an official side event of the Paris AI Action Summit on AI, labour and new policy strategies.</span><span class="meta">Berlin</span></li></ul><p class="year">2024</p><ul class="list"><li><a href="/events/2024-plurality-european-tour/">Plurality European Tour</a><span class="desc">Two weeks of book launches and workshops across Europe with local partners and institutions.</span><span class="meta">Europe</span></li><li><a href="/events/2024-oakland/">What and How We Own: The Politics of Change</a><span class="desc">Seeding a coalition building a new paradigm for property and ownership in the 21st century.</span><span class="meta">Oakland</span></li></ul><p class="year">2023</p><ul class="list"><li><a href="/events/2023-london/">Beyond Cultures of Ownership</a><span class="desc">At Somerset House with Serpentine: how art and culture can reshape our understanding of ownership.</span><span class="meta">London</span></li></ul><p class="year">2022</p><ul class="list"><li><a href="/events/2022-warsaw/">Europe and the Futures of Pluralism</a><span class="desc">With Europe at war, a gathering on the power of diverse cooperation.</span><span class="meta">Warsaw</span></li><li><a href="/events/2022-freedom-games/">Freedom Games</a><span class="desc">RxC panels at the Freedom Games festival.</span><span class="meta">Łódź</span></li><li><a href="/events/2022-bogota/">Plurality Tent at Schelling Point</a><span class="desc">With Fundación Karisma: building a Plurality agenda for democracy and web3.</span><span class="meta">Bogotá</span></li><li><a href="/events/2022-conference/">Exploring Digital Identity for Decentralised Societies</a><span class="desc">Protocols for decentralised social verification as a missing layer of the internet.</span><span class="meta">Online</span></li><li><a href="/events/2022-panels/">2022 Panels</a><span class="desc">Recorded panel series.</span><span class="meta">Online</span></li></ul><p class="year">2021</p><ul class="list"><li><a href="/events/2021-conference/">A New Era of Democracy</a><span class="desc">A participatory conference designed around deliberation and co-creation.</span><span class="meta">Denver and online</span></li><li><a href="/events/2021-panels/">2021 Panels</a><span class="desc">Recorded panel series.</span><span class="meta">Online</span></li></ul><p class="year">2020</p><ul class="list"><li><a href="/events/2020-conference/">2020 Annual Conference</a><span class="desc">The first fully virtual RxC conference.</span><span class="meta">Online</span></li><li><a href="/events/2020-panels/">2020 Panels</a><span class="desc">Recorded panel series.</span><span class="meta">Online</span></li></ul><p class="year">2019</p><ul class="list"><li><a href="/events/2019-berlin/">2019 Berlin Conference</a><span class="desc">RadicalxChange&#x27;s first European conference.</span><span class="meta">Berlin</span></li><li><a href="/events/2019-conference/">2019 Annual Conference</a><span class="desc">The inaugural RadicalxChange conference.</span><span class="meta">Detroit</span></li></ul>
</div></section>
<section class="section tint"><div class="wrap">
<div class="twocol">
<div><h3>For organisations</h3><p>Governments, institutions and community organisations work with the Foundation directly. Publishers, unions and associations who want to bargain collectively with AI companies over their data can <a href="mailto:info@radicalxchange.org?subject=Collective%20data%20bargaining">start here</a>. <a href="/projects/">See how partnerships work</a>, or <a href="mailto:info@radicalxchange.org">get in touch</a>.</p></div>
<div><h3>For builders</h3><p>The tools are open source. Start with <a href="https://quadraticvote.radicalxchange.org/">quadraticvote.radicalxchange.org</a> and the <a href="/wiki/">Library</a>, and bring questions to the monthly call.</p></div>
</div>
